This is a sample to build the kind of database infrastructure we need for Ziniki,
i.e. a combo of neptune and dynamo dbs

    target trial_dbs

The core information (about users and stocks) goes in dynamodb.
Tables are deffo per region, and at some point we need to consider regions.

We have a table of "stock prices" which are basically a symbol and a price.

        ensure aws.DynamoDB.Table "stocks" => stocks_table
            @teardown delete
            Fields<=aws.DynamoFields
                symbol string
                    @Key hash
                price number

And we have a table of users, which (for now) is just a username.

        ensure aws.DynamoDB.Table "users" => users_table
            @teardown delete
            Fields <= aws.DynamoFields
                username string
                    @Key hash

Now, turning to Neptune ...

We need a neptune-specific subnet group.  We should be able to create this, but I did it by hand,
so let's just stick with that for now.

        find aws.Neptune.SubnetGroup "neptunetest" => subnet

Let's create a neptune cluster.  I think this is all you need - a cluster with a name.
After that, everything else seems to be gravy.

        ensure aws.Neptune.Cluster "user-stocks" => neptune
            @teardown delete
            SubnetGroupName <- subnet

